From: xnulinux
Subject: [PATCH] linux64: the sanitizer denylists no longer name the corecrypto files 0008 took out

The KASan and kcov denylists name two files of osfmk/corecrypto one by one (cc_clear.c, ccdrbg_nisthmac.c), and
validate_denylist.sh fails the build when a file a denylist names is missing. Those files are gone with the tree's
corecrypto (0008, vm-xnu-rebuild.sh), so a build into a new object tree stopped in build_setup ("KASan: denylisted
file ... not found"); an object tree from before kept its generated denylists and went on building.
---
--- a/san/coverage/kcov-denylist-x86_64
+++ b/san/coverage/kcov-denylist-x86_64
@@ -3,8 +3,6 @@
 # Early boot AUTOGEN
 src:./bsd/kern/kdebug.c
 src:./bsd/kern/kern_csr.c
-src:./osfmk/corecrypto/cc_clear.c
-src:./osfmk/corecrypto/ccdrbg_nisthmac.c
 src:./osfmk/device/subrs.c
 src:./osfmk/i386/Diagnostics.c
 src:./osfmk/i386/acpi.c
--- a/san/memory/kasan-denylist-x86_64
+++ b/san/memory/kasan-denylist-x86_64
@@ -5,8 +5,6 @@
 # Early boot AUTOGEN
 src:./bsd/kern/kdebug.c
 src:./bsd/kern/kern_csr.c
-src:./osfmk/corecrypto/cc_clear.c
-src:./osfmk/corecrypto/ccdrbg_nisthmac.c
 src:./osfmk/device/subrs.c
 src:./osfmk/i386/Diagnostics.c
 src:./osfmk/i386/acpi.c
